A :PARAMETERS keyword with no names fires diag.empty_parameters (error, on
the keyword), at script level and inside a procedure.
-- input.ssl --
:PARAMETERS;
:PROCEDURE Ping;
	:PARAMETERS;
	:RETURN .T.;
:ENDPROC;
:RETURN DoProc("Ping");
-- format --
:PARAMETERS;

:PROCEDURE Ping;
	:PARAMETERS;

	:RETURN .T.;
:ENDPROC;

:RETURN DoProc("Ping");
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:12 error empty_parameters: ':PARAMETERS' must name at least one parameter; leave the line out when there are none
3:2-3:13 error empty_parameters: ':PARAMETERS' must name at least one parameter; leave the line out when there are none
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:12 error empty_parameters: ':PARAMETERS' must name at least one parameter; leave the line out when there are none
3:2-3:13 error empty_parameters: ':PARAMETERS' must name at least one parameter; leave the line out when there are none
